.TH @PACKAGE_TARNAME@.conf 5
.SH NAME
@PACKAGE_TARNAME@.conf - @PACKAGE_NAME@ Configuration File Format v@PACKAGE_VERSION@
.SH DESCRIPTION
The @PACKAGE_TARNAME@.conf file...
.IP \(bu 2
follows the standard INI-style format.
.IP \(bu 2
contains configuration parameters for \fB@PACKAGE_TARNAME@(8)\fR, a deep-packet inspection server.
.IP \(bu 2
contains configuration parameters for the
.UR https://www.netify.ai/products/netify-informatics
Netify Informatics
.UE service.
.SS Main
The main server options are defined within the [\fB@PACKAGE_TARNAME@\fR] section.
.PP
\fBauto_informatics\fR=\fIBOOLEAN\fR
.PP
Enable automatic Netify Informatics integration.  This option is intended to be managed exclusively by the \-\-enable/disable\-informatics command\-line parameters.
.PP
\fBprofile\fR=\fIPATH\fR
.PP
Configuration profile to load from \fIPATH\fR.  This is typically used to override defaults set in the main configuration file.
.PP
\fBpath_state_persistent\fR=\fIPATH\fR
.PP
Where to store "persistent" data (configuration files, etc).  The default is /etc/@PACKAGE_TARNAME@
.PP
\fBpath_state_volatile\fR=\fIPATH\fR
.PP
Where to store "volatile" data (temporary state files, etc).  The default is /var/run/@PACKAGE_TARNAME@
.PP
\fBuser\fR=\fIUSER\fR, \fBgroup\fR=\fIGROUP\fR
.PP
Switch to non-root user and/or group on start-up.  Requires Linux Capabilities support to be enabled at compile time.
.PP
\fBmax_capture_length\fR=\fIINTEGER\fR
.PP
The maximum number of bytes to capture (copy) per packet.  The maximum value is 65535, which is also the default.
.PP
\fBmax_detection_pkts\fR=\fIINTEGER\fR
.PP
This option controls the number of packets that are examined by the DPI engine before taking a guess at the type of flow.  The smaller the value the less processing overhead but the less likely enough of a conversation will be analyzed, resulting in fewer detections.  The default value is 32 packets.
.PP
\fBmax_flows\fR=\fIINTEGER\fR
.PP
The maximum number of flows to track at any given moment.  When this value has been reached, new flows will stop being tracked until old flows expire.  The default is 0 (unlimited).
.PP
\fBupdate_interval\fR=\fISECONDS\fR
.PP
How often (in seconds) to process the global flow maps.  Flow statistics are made available, idle flows are expired, and other house-keeping is performed during this update period.  The default is 15s.
.PP
\fBttl_idle_flow\fR=\fISECONDS\fR, \fBttl_idle_tcp_flow\fR=\fISECONDS\fR
.PP
How long to wait (in seconds) until an idle flow (non-TCP or TCP) is scheduled for expiry.
.PP
\fBauto_flow_expiry\fR=\fIBOOLEAN\fR
.PP
On shutdown, force flows to immediately expire.  The default is yes.
.PP
\fBsyn_scan_protection\fR=\fIBOOLEAN\fR
.PP
Don't track TCP flows until a SYN+ACK has been captured.
.PP
\fBsoft_dissectors\fR=\fIBOOLEAN\fR
.PP
Enable or disable Soft-dissectors (flow expressions defined in the application signatures).
.PP
\fBflow_map_buckets\fR=\fIINTEGER\fR
.PP
The number of "buckets" the main flow map will be divided into.  The default is 128.
.PP
\fBnetwork_namespace\fR=\fINAME/PID/PATH\fR
.PP
Attach to an alternate network namespace.
.PP
\fBpath_server_socket\fR=\fIPATH\fR
.PP
Local command/control socket.  Receive commands and control messages on a local UNIX socket.
.PP
\fBuse_getifaddrs\fR=\fIBOOLEAN\fR
.PP
Periodically call getifaddrs(3) to update the associated IP addresses of each capture source.
.PP
.SS Threads
Threading options are defined within the [\fBthreads\fR] section.
.PP
\fBcapture_base\fR=\fIINTEGER\fR
.PP
Base CPU ID to start capture threads from.
.PP
\fBdetection_base\fR=\fIINTEGER\fR
.PP
Base CPU ID to start detection threads from.
.PP
\fBdetection_cores\fR=\fIINTEGER\fR
.PP
Number of detection (DPI) threads to start.
.PP
.SS Netlink
Linux Netlink and Conntrack options are defined within the [\fBnetlink\fR] section.
.PP
\fBbuffer_size\fR=\fIINTEGER\fR
.PP
Set the Netlink buffer size.
.PP
\fBconntrack_buffer_size\fR=\fIINTEGER\fR
.PP
Set the Conntrack buffer size.
.PP
\fBconntrack_idle_ttl\fR=\fISECONDS\fR
.PP
In the event we miss a conntrack DESTROY event, clean-up cached flow entries that have been idle for greater than this number of seconds.
.PP
\fBbridge_pvid_discovery\fR=\fIBOOLEAN\fR
.PP
Enable Bridge PVID discovery.
.PP
.SS Capture Defaults
Capture source defaults are set under a [\fBcapture-defaults\fR] section.
.PP
\fBcapture_type\fR=\fITYPE\fR
.PP
Specify the packet capture type.  Depending on the platform and compile-time options, valid capture types are: \fBpcap\fR, \fBtpv3\fR, or \fBnfqueue\fR.
.PP
\fBread_timeout\fR=\fIMILLISECONDS\fR
.PP
Packet capture timeout value (milliseconds).
.PP
.SS TPv3 Capture Defaults
Linux TPv3 specific defaults are set under a [\fBcapture-defaults-tpv3\fR] section.
.PP
\fBfanout_mode\fR=\fIMODE\fR
.PP
Set the fanout mode: hash, lb, cpu, rollover, or random.
.PP
\fBfanout_flags\fR=\fIFLAGS\fR
.PP
Set the fanout flags: defrag, rollover.
.PP
\fBfanout_instances\fR=\fIINTEGER\fR
.PP
Set the number of fanout instances.
.PP
\fBrb_block_size\fR=\fIINTEGER\fR, \fBrb_frame_size\fR=\fIINTEGER\fR, \fBrb_blocks\fR=\fIINTEGER\fR
.PP
Set the ring buffer block size, frame size, and number of blocks.
.PP
.SS Capture Interfaces
Individual capture interface options can be set under sections named [\fBcapture-interface-\fIINTERFACE\fR].
.PP
\fBenable\fR=\fIBOOLEAN\fR
.PP
Enable or disable capture on this interface.
.PP
\fBrole\fR=\fILAN | WAN\fR
.PP
Specify the role of the interface (internal or external).
.PP
\fBaddress\fR[\fIn\fR]=\fIADDRESS\fR
.PP
Specify local IP addresses for the interface.
.PP
\fBpeer\fR=\fIINTERFACE\fR
.PP
Associate the interface with a peer interface.
.PP
\fBfilter\fR=\fIBPF\fR
.PP
Attach a BPF filter expression to the interface.
.PP
.SS DNS Hint Cache
DNS hint cache options are set within the [\fBdns_hint_cache\fR] section.

The DNS hint cache stores DNS response records for a period of time.  These hints are used when application detection fails.  A cache look-up is performed and any matching hostname is used to 'hint' the application detection logic.  In most cases this significantly improves application detection.
.PP
\fBenable\fR=\fIBOOLEAN\fR
.PP
Enable or disable the DNS hint cache.  On non-embedded systems with more memory, it is highly recommended that this be enabled for more comprehensive application detection.  The default is true.
.PP
\fBpartial_lookups\fR=\fIBOOLEAN\fR
.PP
Enable or disable partial DNS lookups.
.PP
\fBsave\fR=\fIpersistent\fR | \fIvolatile\fR | \fIdisabled\fR
.PP
Enable or disable periodic saving of the DNS hint cache.  The default is: \fIpersistent\fR
.PP
\fBcache_size\fR=\fIINTEGER\fR
.PP
The maximum number of entries to store in the DNS hint cache.
.PP
.SS Flow Hash Cache
Flow hash cache options are set within the [\fBflow-hash-cache\fR] section.
.PP
\fBenable\fR=\fIBOOLEAN\fR
.PP
Enable or disable the flow hash cache.
.PP
\fBsave\fR=\fIpersistent\fR | \fIvolatile\fR | \fIdisabled\fR
.PP
Enable or disable periodic saving of the flow hash cache.
.PP
\fBcache_size\fR=\fIINTEGER\fR
.PP
The maximum number of entries to store in the flow hash cache.
.PP
.SS Netify API
Netify API integration options are defined within the [\fBnetify-api\fR] section.
.PP
\fBenable\fR=\fIBOOLEAN\fR
.PP
Enable or disable API integration with Netify Informatics.
.PP
\fBupdate_tick\fR=\fISECONDS\fR
.PP
Frequency of internal API housekeeping.
.PP
\fBupdate_interval\fR=\fISECONDS\fR
.PP
Interval for updating application and category data from the API server.
.PP
\fBbootstrap_url\fR=\fIURL\fR
.PP
URL for the initial API bootstrap process.
.PP
\fBvendor\fR=\fINAME\fR
.PP
Vendor name to use for API identification.
.PP
\fBtls_verify\fR=\fIBOOLEAN\fR
.PP
Verify TLS certificates for API connections.
.PP
\fBmtls_enable\fR=\fIBOOLEAN\fR
.PP
Enable or disable mTLS (mutual TLS) authentication for API connections.
.PP
\fBcert_file\fR=\fIPATH\fR
.PP
Path to the client certificate file for mTLS authentication.
.PP
\fBkey_file\fR=\fIPATH\fR
.PP
Path to the client private key file for mTLS authentication.
.PP
.SS Protocols
Protocol dissector options are defined within the [\fBprotocols\fR] section.
.PP
\fB\fIprotocol_tag\fR\fR=\fIinclude | exclude\fR
.PP
Enable or disable specific DPI protocol dissectors by their tag.  Use \fBall=include\fR to enable all known dissectors.
.PP
.SS Privacy Filter
The @PACKAGE_NAME@ can be configured to obfuscate flow addresses (MAC and IP) that match rules in the [\fBprivacy-filter\fR] section.
.PP
\fBmac\fR[\fIn\fR]\fR=\fIMAC\fR
.PP
Privacy filter by MAC address.
.PP
\fBhost\fR[\fIn\fR]\fR=\fIADDRESS\fR
.PP
Privacy filter by IP address.
.PP
\fBregex_search\fR[\fIn\fR]\fR=\fIREGEX\fR, \fBregex_replace\fR[\fIn\fR]\fR=\fISTRING\fR
.PP
Search for a regular expression in flow metadata and replace it with a string.
.PP
\fBprivate_external_addresses\fR=\fIBOOLEAN\fR
.PP
Obfuscate external IP addresses in flows.
.SH SAMPLE CONFIGURATION
The following sample configuration file contains most common options with their default values.

.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# @PACKAGE_NAME@ sample configuration for version @PACKAGE_VERSION@

[@PACKAGE_TARNAME@]
# profile = @persistentstatedir@/profiles.d/00-default.conf
update_interval = 15
max_flows = 0

[capture-defaults]
capture_type = pcap

[threads]
# capture_base = 0
# detection_base = 1
# detection_cores = 2

[flow-hash-cache]
enable = yes
save = persistent
cache_size = 1000

[dns_hint_cache]
enable = yes
save = persistent
cache_size = 1000

[netify-api]
enable = no
# mtls_enable = no
# cert_file = /etc/netifyd/client-cert.pem
# key_file = /etc/netifyd/client-key.pem

[protocols]
all = include

[netlink]
conntrack_idle_ttl = 3600

[privacy_filter]
# host[0] = 192.168.1.1
.EE
.in
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
@PACKAGE_TARNAME@(8)
